.TH JPACKER 8 "June 2026" "jpacker @VERSION@" "System Administration Utilities"
.SH NAME
jpacker \- A robust Pacman wrapper and AUR helper with source-based build management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jpacker
.I <operation>
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ targets... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jpacker
is a C++20 pacman wrapper and AUR helper.
It extends pacman's functionality by handling AUR packages, providing one-off source builds for official packages, and managing persistent per-package source build preferences (similar to Gentoo's package.env).

Operations handled entirely by pacman pass through pacman-compatible options that jpacker does not consume.
When a sync target is routed to AUR or a source build, pacman options that cannot retain their meaning during makepkg build/install are rejected before the transaction starts instead of being ignored.
Pacman options that take values must follow the operation and may use either \fB--option value\fR or \fB--option=value\fR form. A missing value for an option tracked by jpacker stops before pacman execution.
Unsupported options for jpacker-specific operations also stop instead of being forwarded to pacman.

.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B \-S, \-Syu, \-Syy
Install packages or update the system. If a target is found in the official repositories, pacman is used. If not, it is searched in the AUR.
If a package has a source-build preference (via \fBadd-src\fR), it will be built from source even if it exists in the official repositories.
\fBjpacker -Syu\fR is treated as a pacman-compatible system upgrade and does not scan all registered source-build preferences. Use \fBjpacker upgrade\fR when registered source-build settings should be checked after the system upgrade and rebuilt when needed.
\fBjpacker -Sc\fR is passed through to \fBsudo pacman -Sc\fR and cleans pacman caches only. Use \fBjpacker clean\fR when you also want to remove jpacker build/cache files.
The jpacker cache directory is \fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/jpacker\fR when \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR is set, otherwise \fI$HOME/.cache/jpacker\fR.
\fBjpacker clean\fR shows the resolved jpacker cache directory at runtime and removes cached build files after confirmation. \fIjpacker.log\fR is excluded.
.TP
.B \-Ss \fI<query>\fR
Search for packages in both the official repositories and the AUR.
AUR search results may show status tags such as \fB[installed]\fR, \fB[out-of-date]\fR, and \fB[orphaned]\fR when that metadata is available.
When refresh is requested with \fB-y\fR or \fB--refresh\fR, the official repository search uses \fBsudo pacman\fR before the usual AUR search.
.TP
.B \-Si \fI<package>\fR
Show package information. Official repository packages use pacman output; AUR packages use AUR metadata and include installed, orphaned, and out-of-date state.
When refresh is requested, every target must use a repository-qualified form such as \fBcore/filesystem\fR. An unqualified target stops before pacman, sudo, or an AUR query so an official database refresh cannot run before a possible AUR fallback is known. Without refresh, the existing repository-first AUR fallback remains available.
.TP
.B \-F, \-Fl \fI<query>\fR
Search or list the pacman file database without sudo. Forms that request a file database refresh, including \fB-Fy\fR, \fB-Fyy\fR, \fB-F -y\fR, and \fB-F --refresh\fR, use \fBsudo pacman\fR.
.TP
.B \-R, \-Rs, \-Rns \fI<target>\fR
Remove packages. This is a direct wrapper around \fBpacman -R\fR.
.TP
.B build \fI<package> [VAR=VALUE...]\fR
Perform a one-off build from source for a package (either from Official Repos or AUR).
Environment variables (like CFLAGS) can be passed directly.
.br
Example: \fIjpacker build coreutils CFLAGS="-O3 -march=native"\fR
.TP
.B deps [\-\-recursive] \fI<package>\fR
Inspect an AUR package's runtime, make, and check dependencies, then classify them as official repository dependencies, AUR dependencies, provided dependencies, ambiguous provider candidates, or unknown dependencies.
With \fB\-\-recursive\fR, recursively inspect AUR dependencies. Official repository, provided, ambiguous, and unknown dependencies are shown but not traversed.
If exactly one provider is found, it may be shown as a provided dependency. If multiple providers are found, jpacker reports the dependency as ambiguous and does not choose one implicitly.
Version constraints such as \fBfoo>=1.2\fR are detected and shown, but jpacker v1.x does not verify them with a complete pacman/libalpm-compatible solver.
If the target package declares AUR \fBConflicts\fR or \fBReplaces\fR metadata, it is shown separately as a metadata warning. This warning does not change the command's successful inspection status.
This command does not clone, build, install dependencies, or calculate build order.
.TP
.B plan \fI<package>\fR
Display a build order plan for an AUR package and its recursive AUR dependencies.
Official repository and repository-provided dependencies are not included in the build plan. Unknown dependencies are reported as unresolved.
If multiple providers remain for a dependency, the plan is reported as incomplete with ambiguous provider candidates; jpacker does not choose one implicitly.
Unverified version constraints are reported as unresolved reasons and are not treated as satisfied.
If the requested AUR package has a package name different from its PackageBase, the plan shows it as a split package install target and reports the plan as incomplete because install target selection is not implemented.
Conflicts/replaces metadata for every AUR package in the recursive plan is shown with its package name. A plan containing this metadata is incomplete because jpacker v1.x does not resolve it automatically.
This command does not clone, build, or install dependencies.
.TP
.B fetch \fI<package>\fR
Safely retrieve the AUR build repositories needed to inspect an AUR package and its recursive AUR dependencies before any build/install stage.
Fetch targets are resolved by PackageBase. Official repository and provided dependencies are not cloned. Unknown dependencies are reported as unresolved.
Split package install target selection is not required for fetch itself; if the requested package resolves to a PackageBase and the fetch plan has no unresolved, ambiguous, or cyclic issue, fetch may still clone or fetch that PackageBase.
Conflicts/replaces metadata is shown as a warning but does not prevent fetch, because fetch is limited to read-only repository retrieval.
Missing AUR repositories are cloned. Existing cloned repositories run only \fBgit fetch origin\fR.
This command does not update the working tree and does not run \fBgit pull\fR, merge, reset, build, or install operations.
Future behavior that advances a working tree is not implemented by \fBfetch\fR and should be considered in a separate issue as a command or option such as \fBsync\fR, \fBupdate\fR, or \fBfetch --update\fR.
.TP
.B upgrade
Perform a system upgrade and configured rebuilds. This first runs \fBsudo pacman -Syu\fR, then checks packages with source-build preferences and rebuilds them from source only when the version in the existing \fI.SRCINFO\fR is newer than the installed package.
Use this command, not \fBjpacker -Syu\fR, when registered source-build settings in \fI/etc/jpacker/package.build/\fR should be checked automatically after a system upgrade.
During existing cache repository updates, jpacker can show \fBHEAD..origin/<branch>\fR before resetting the working tree. Initial clones have no previous checkout to compare against, so no update diff prompt is shown.
Before build/install, jpacker prompts to review \fIPKGBUILD\fR and reports top-level \fI*.install\fR files when present. This does not evaluate \fIPKGBUILD\fR to resolve \fBinstall=\fR; it only highlights install scripts already present in the working tree.
\fBjpacker upgrade\fR uses the existing \fI.SRCINFO\fR in the working tree for pre-review update checks. If \fI.SRCINFO\fR is missing or incomplete, jpacker does not run \fBmakepkg --printsrcinfo\fR before review; interactive runs ask whether to continue, while \fB--noconfirm\fR or non-interactive runs skip the package.
.TP
.B clean
Clean package/build caches. This first runs \fBsudo pacman -Sc\fR to clean the official package cache, and then prompts to remove cached build files from the resolved jpacker cache directory. The directory is \fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/jpacker\fR when \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR is set, otherwise \fI$HOME/.cache/jpacker\fR. \fIjpacker.log\fR is preserved.
.TP
.B add-src \fI<package> [VAR=VALUE...]\fR
Enable a source-build preference for a package. This creates a preference file in \fI/etc/jpacker/package.build/\fR.
You can optionally append build environment variables to the preference.
.TP
.B del-src \fI<package>\fR
Remove a source-build preference. Removes the preference file.
.TP
.B revert \fI<package>\fR
Remove a source-build preference AND immediately reinstall the official binary version (via \fBpacman -S\fR) if the package exists in the official repositories. Use this to restore a package to its standard state.
.TP
.B edit-src \fI<package>\fR
Open the source-build preference file for the specified package using the defined \fBEDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B list-src
List source-build preferences along with their custom environment variables.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-noedit
Skip the interactive review/edit of \fIPKGBUILD\fR and top-level \fI*.install\fR files before building.
.TP
.BR \-\-nodiff
Skip the interactive git diff check during existing cache repository updates.
.TP
.BR \-\-noconfirm
Pass \fB--noconfirm\fR to pacman and makepkg execution. jpacker treats this as a request to avoid interactive blocking, not as "yes to everything". This does not bypass jpacker's ambiguous provider, unresolved dependency, cyclic build plan, split package install target, or conflicts/replaces metadata checks.
.TP
.BR \-\-rebuild
Pass \fB-f\fR to makepkg build/install execution so existing built package artifacts are not reused. When omitted, jpacker may ask before rebuilding an existing local package artifact; the default answer is no.
.TP
.BR \-\-cleanbuild
Pass \fB-C\fR to makepkg build/install execution so the existing \fIsrcdir\fR is not reused. When omitted, jpacker may ask before cleaning an existing local \fIsrc/\fR directory; the default answer is no. If a local package artifact exists in the same package directory, cleanbuild also enables rebuild.
.TP
.BR \-\-rmdeps
Pass \fB-r\fR to AUR/source-build makepkg execution. This is explicit opt-in and is not enabled by \fB--noconfirm\fR alone. makepkg removes only dependencies it installed through \fB-s\fR after a successful build; jpacker does not run its own pacman removal or orphan cleanup. This option is not passed to pacman-only installs.
.PP
AUR/source build installation uses \fBmakepkg -sic\fR as its baseline. \fB--noconfirm\fR adds the same makepkg option, while \fB--rebuild\fR, \fB--cleanbuild\fR, and \fB--rmdeps\fR add \fB-f\fR, \fB-C\fR, and \fB-r\fR respectively. Other pacman transaction options are not translated to makepkg; if an AUR/source-build target is present, unsupported options stop the invocation before pacman or makepkg execution.
.PP
jpacker v1.x does not compare AUR conflicts/replaces metadata with installed or official repository packages, use replacements to select install targets, or automatically remove or replace packages. Any AUR build/install plan containing this metadata stops before clone, fetch, build, makepkg, or a pacman transaction.
.TP
.BR \-h , \ \-\-help
Display the help message and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
The main configuration file is located at \fI/etc/jpacker/jpacker.conf\fR.
It supports the following keys:
.TP
.B NOEDIT
Set to \fBtrue\fR to disable \fIPKGBUILD\fR / \fI*.install\fR review prompts globally.
.TP
.B NODIFF
Set to \fBtrue\fR to disable git diff checks during existing cache repository updates globally.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Specify the preferred text editor. The priority is the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable, this configuration value, then \fBnano\fR.
Editor command tokens are restricted to simple command words and simple options for safety. For example, \fBnano\fR, \fBvim\fR, and \fBcode --wait\fR are supported. Complex shell syntax such as shell expansion, nested quoting, pipes, redirects, or command chains is intentionally unsupported.
.TP
.B LOGFILE
Specify the path to the log file. Supports tilde expansion (e.g., \fB~/logs/jpacker.log\fR).
Default is \fI~/.cache/jpacker/jpacker.log\fR.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/jpacker/jpacker.conf
Global configuration file. Controls editor settings, log locations, and review prompts.
.TP
.I /etc/jpacker/package.build/
Directory containing source-build preference files managed with \fBadd-src\fR.
Each file corresponds to a package name and can define environment variables (e.g., CFLAGS) that are applied during \fBmakepkg\fR execution.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/jpacker/
Default directory used for downloading and building packages when \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR is not set. If \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR is set, jpacker uses \fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/jpacker\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/jpacker/jpacker.log
Default log file location.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/jpacker
Bash completion file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_jpacker
zsh completion file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/jpacker.fish
fish completion file.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
The editor used for reviewing PKGBUILDs and editing configurations.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Used to determine the build directory location.

.SH EXAMPLES
.B Update the system and packages with source-build preferences:
.RS
jpacker upgrade
.RE

.B Update the system without scanning registered source-build preferences:
.RS
jpacker -Syu
.RE

.B Install a package from AUR without review:
.RS
jpacker -S google-chrome --noedit
.RE

.B Install a package without pacman/makepkg confirmation prompts:
.RS
jpacker --noconfirm -S google-chrome
.RE

.B Classify dependencies of an AUR package:
.RS
jpacker deps google-chrome
.RE

.B Recursively inspect AUR dependencies:
.RS
jpacker deps --recursive google-chrome
.RE

.B Show a build order plan for an AUR package:
.RS
jpacker plan mongodb-bin
.RE

.B Safely clone or fetch AUR build repositories:
.RS
jpacker fetch mongodb-bin
.RE

.B Enable a source-build preference with custom optimizations:
.RS
jpacker add-src neofetch CFLAGS="-O3 -march=native"
.RE

.B Clean caches to free up space:
.RS
jpacker clean
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8)
.PP
For the detailed operation and option pass-through policy, see the repository document \fIdocs/COMPATIBILITY.md\fR.

.SH AUTHOR
Written by seekerkrt.
